cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this study or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "The Calibration Cost of the MLX Quantization Ladder"
authors:
  - family-names: "Durukan"
    given-names: "Mert"
    email: "mert@durukan.dev"
type: software
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21596523
repository-code: "https://github.com/mertdurukan/mlx-quantization-calibration"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-07-26
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered study of how MLX post-training quantization
  (bf16 to 8/6/5/4/3/2-bit affine, mxfp4, and four mixed-bit recipes)
  affects LLM confidence calibration, as distinct from accuracy.
  All four pre-registered hypotheses are falsified as stated; the
  full mechanical verdict trail, per-item measurements, and analysis
  code are included.
keywords:
  - quantization
  - calibration
  - large language models
  - MLX
  - Apple Silicon
  - expected calibration error
  - pre-registered research
